        <div class="jcBand">
            <div id="pnlJobDescription">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span>For questions related to the duties of the position, contact Assistant Chief Bo Lee at (408) 472-1602 or Bo.Lee@fire.ca.gov.</span></span><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><a href="mailto:peter.avansino@fire.ca.gov" style="text-decoration-line: none;"><span style="color: #0563c1; text-decoration-line: underline;"></span></a></span></p><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=25734151&name=SCUPO-199FCP.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
</div>

            <div id="pnlWorkingConditions">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Working Conditions</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">The incumbent is required to wear respiratory protection equipment (including self-contained breathing apparatus (SCBA). The use of such equipment may place a physiological burden on the incumbent that varies with the type of equipment used, the job and workplace conditions in which the equipment is used, and the medical status of the incumbent. As such, Cal/OSHA requires that the incumbent be annually medically cleared to be fit-tested for respiratory protection equipment. This clearance process consists of a comprehensive medical evaluation including a review of the incumbent&#39;s medical history, a complete physical examination, and vision, hearing, spirometry, and exercise treadmill test.</span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">The incumbent typically is required to perform psychologically stressful and/or physically demanding duties consistent with firefighting, disaster response, and emergency medical response, including working in isolated areas, walking or running on uneven rough terrain, and remaining on duty 24 hours or longer without a break while performing these duties.</span></p>
                </p>
            
</div>
        </div>

